---
// Illustrative story: layout and fields mirror the app's story view; the event is invented.
const sources = [0.18, 0.31, 0.42, 0.47, 0.5, 0.55, 0.61, 0.7, 0.84];
const checks = [
  { claim: 'Temperatures will reach 39 °C in the south', verdict: 'confirmat', en: 'confirmed · 3 outlets', tone: 'ok' },
  { claim: 'Water restrictions start in two counties', verdict: 'o singură sursă', en: 'single source', tone: 'single' },
  { claim: 'Schools will close on Friday', verdict: 'contestat', en: 'contested · 1 outlet disagrees', tone: 'bad' },
];
---

<figure class="story" data-reveal>
  <div class="frame">
    <header class="top">
      <span class="label">Story · 9 sources · 6 RO, 3 intl.</span>
      <span class="chip importance">Importance 7.4</span>
    </header>
    <h3 class="title">Cod galben de caniculă prelungit în sudul țării</h3>
    <p class="en muted">Heat warning extended across southern Romania</p>

    <div class="summary">
      <p lang="ro">
        Avertizarea de caniculă a fost prelungită până duminică pentru 14 județe. Sursele sunt de acord asupra
        temperaturilor și duratei, dar diferă privind măsurile pentru școli.
      </p>
      <p class="muted en-t">
        The heat warning has been extended to Sunday for 14 counties. Sources agree on temperatures and duration, but
        differ on measures for schools.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="meters">
      <div class="meter">
        <p class="label">Bias spectrum</p>
        <div class="spectrum" role="img" aria-label="Nine sources spread from left to right, clustered around the centre">
          {sources.map((s) => <span class="dot" style={`left:${s * 100}%`} />)}
        </div>
        <div class="scale label"><span>Left</span><span>Centre</span><span>Right</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="meter">
        <p class="label">Consensus</p>
        <div class="bar"><span style="width:78%"></span></div>
        <p class="val"><strong>78%</strong> <span class="muted">high agreement</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kv">
      <div>
        <p class="label">What we know</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Warning covers 14 counties</li>
          <li>Valid until Sunday, 22:00</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="label">Still unclear</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Whether schools will close</li>
          <li>Impact on the power grid</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="checks">
      <p class="label">Fact-check · verdicts computed from other outlets</p>
      <ul>
        {
          checks.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <span class="claim">{c.claim}</span>
              <span class={`verdict ${c.tone}`} lang="ro">
                {c.verdict}
              </span>
              <span class="muted en-v">{c.en}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="muted">Illustrative sample. The fields and layout match the app's story view; the event is invented.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .story {
    margin-block: 40px;
  }
  .frame {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: var(--color-deep);
  }
  .top {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .importance {
    color: var(--color-ice);
  }
  .title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.6vw, 1.8rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .en {
    margin-top: -14px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .summary {
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
    padding-left: 16px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-ice);
  }
  .en-t {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  .meters {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
  }
  .meter .label {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .spectrum {
    position: relative;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #6f86ff, #3a4a6e 50%, #ff8a6f);
  }
  .dot {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    margin: -6px 0 0 -6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-frost);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-deep);
  }
  .scale {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
  }
  .bar {
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-line);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .bar span {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-ice), var(--color-aurora));
  }
  .val {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .kv {
    display: grid;
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .kv ul {
    margin-top: 8px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .kv li::before {
    content: '— ';
    color: var(--color-mist);
  }
  .checks ul {
    display: grid;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  .checks li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 4px 12px;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: 12px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .claim {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .verdict {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    padding: 0.3em 0.7em;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .verdict.ok {
    color: var(--color-aurora);
  }
  .verdict.single {
    color: var(--color-ice);
  }
  .verdict.bad {
    color: var(--color-ember);
  }
  .en-v {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .meters,
    .kv {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }
</style>
